const GLOSS={'P/E':'Price ÷ yearly profit per share. 20 means investors pay $20 for every $1 the company earns in a year. Higher usually means people expect fast growth.','P/E ratio':'Price ÷ yearly profit per share. 20 means investors pay $20 for every $1 the company earns in a year.','Beta':'How much the stock tends to move compared with the whole market. 1 = same as the market, 2 = twice as much, 0.5 = half as much.','Market cap':'What the whole company is worth on the stock market: share price × number of shares.','52-week range':'The lowest and highest price over the past year.','Dividend yield':'Cash the company pays shareholders each year, as a % of the share price.','Previous close':'The price when the market closed on the last trading day.','Day change':'How much the price has moved today, in %.','Day range':'The lowest and highest price so far today.','Volume':'How many shares changed hands today. High volume means lots of interest.','Net margin':'How many cents of profit the company keeps from each dollar of sales.','1-year return':'How much the price has gone up or down over the past 12 months.','Sector':'The industry the company belongs to.','Equity':'What your paper account is worth right now: cash plus everything you own at today’s prices.','Cash (buying power)':'Virtual cash you can still spend.','Open P/L':'Profit or loss on what you still own, if you sold it all right now.','Realized P/L':'Profit or loss you locked in by selling.','Total return':'How much your account is up or down since you started with $100,000.'};
